.TH EPHER 1  "epher 0.4.30" "User Commands"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
epher \- A programmable, scriptable calculator.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBepher\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIEXPRESSION\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
A programmable, scriptable calculator. One engine, five ways to use it: a one\-shot command (`epher "2 + 3"`), an interactive session (`epher repl`), a full\-screen terminal UI (`epher tui`), a desktop app (`epher gui`), and an offline web app at https://epher.org/pwa/. All five speak the same language.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIEXPRESSION\fR]
A script to evaluate; each statement\*(Aqs result prints on its own line.

Anything from the language works — `2 + 3 * 4`, `if 3 > 2 then 1 else 0`, a leading minus — and statements join with `;` or newlines: `epher "x = 10; x + 5"` prints `10` then `15`. Use `\-` to read a script from standard input, line by line, instead. `graph`/`graph3d` statements plot too; `graph save file.svg` writes the plot as an SVG image (`epher "graph sin(x); graph save plot.svg"`).
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
epher\-repl(1)
Start an interactive session in the terminal
.TP
epher\-tui(1)
Start the full\-screen terminal interface
.TP
epher\-gui(1)
Start the desktop app
.TP
epher\-help(1)
Print the manual, or help for a subcommand
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "THE EPHER LANGUAGE"
epher evaluates arithmetic with the usual precedence: factorial (!) binds strongest, then power (^, right to left), then * and /, then + and \-. Parentheses group. Numbers may use scientific notation (6.02e23). The constants pi, e, tau, and phi are always available.
Comparison and logic:
.TP 4
a > b, < >= <= == !=
comparisons (true/false)
.TP 4
and, or, not
logical connectives
Statements:
.TP 4
name = value
assign a variable (x = 5)
.TP 4
const name = value
define a constant (const tax = 0.2); immutable, visible everywhere, saved with `save`
.TP 4
if c then a else b
conditional expression
.TP 4
while c do statement
loop
.TP 4
def name(params) = expr
define a function; recursion works (def fib(n) = if n <= 1 then n else fib(n \- 1) + fib(n \- 2))
.TP 4
stmt1; stmt2
a script: statements joined with `;` or newlines (the same separator)
Exact layers (binary floats are exact here):
.TP 4
frac(n, d)
exact fraction (frac(1, 3) = 1/3)
.TP 4
dec(x)
exact decimal (dec(0.1) + dec(0.2) = 0.3)
.TP 4
big(x)
exact whole number (big(10 ^ 20))
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "BUILT-IN FUNCTIONS"
Trigonometry works in radians; deg(x) and rad(x) convert.
.TP 4
sin cos tan asin acos atan atan2
trigonometric and inverse trigonometric
.TP 4
deg(x), rad(x)
radians to degrees and back
.TP 4
sinh cosh tanh asinh acosh atanh
hyperbolic and inverse hyperbolic
.TP 4
sqrt cbrt root(n, x) exp
powers and roots
.TP 4
ln log log2 logb(b, x) hypot(a, b)
logarithms and hypotenuse
.TP 4
n! or fact(n)
factorial
.TP 4
abs floor ceil round trunc sign
rounding and sign
.TP 4
mod(a, b) gcd(a, b) lcm(a, b)
remainders and common divisors
.TP 4
ncr(n, r), npr(n, r)
combinations and permutations
.TP 4
sum product mean median min max variance stdev
statistics over any number of arguments
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SHELL COMMANDS"
Inside the interactive session (repl) and piped scripts, these lines are shell commands, not expressions:
.TP 4
save name
save the function or constant `name` for future sessions
.TP 4
save script name
save the last evaluated line as a script
.TP 4
graph expr [from a to b]
plot a curve (cartesian, param, polar; regions with y < / y >); the curves accumulate
.TP 4
graph3d z = f(x, y) [from a to b]
plot a 3D surface
.TP 4
graph save file.svg | graph3d save file.svg
write the current plot as a self\-contained SVG image
.TP 4
graph clear | graph3d clear
empty the plot
.TP 4
language code
set the interface language: en, zh\-CN, hi, es, fr, ar, de, pt
.TP 4
table expr [from a to b] [points n]
print a table of values (TI\-style defaults: \-5..5, 11 rows)
.TP 4
quit, exit
leave the interactive session (Ctrl\-D too)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP 4
0
success
.TP 4
1
a calculation or runtime error
.TP 4
2
usage error (bad arguments; also when `epher \-` finds a terminal on stdin)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH FILES
.TP 4
~/.epher/
the epher store: saved functions, constants, scripts, history, and the language preference. Delete it to start fresh.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP 4
EPHER_STORE_DIR
relocate the store (EPHER_STORE_DIR=/tmp/scratch epher repl)
.TP 4
NO_COLOR
disable colored error output when set (see no\-color.org)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP 4
epher "2 + 3 * 4"
print the value of an expression: 14
.TP 4
epher "x = 10; x + 5"
scripts work too: each statement\*(Aqs value prints (10 then 15)
.TP 4
epher "\-2 + 5"
a leading minus is part of the expression; prints 3
.TP 4
printf "x = 3\\nx * 10\\n" | epher \-
read a script from standard input, line by line
.TP 4
printf "def f(x) = x ^ 2\\nf(9)\\n" | epher \-
lines share one session: prints = 81
.TP 4
epher repl
interactive session; answers print as `= result`
.TP 4
epher tui
full\-screen interface with graphing (graph x ^ 2, graph3d x ^ 2 \- y ^ 2, space animates)
